{"case_id":"C047","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["configuration","state","API protocol","input semantics","entry point"],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["ares_init_options","init_by_options","init_by_environment","init_by_resolv_conf","set_options","set_search","ares_getaddrinfo","next_dns_lookup","ares_getsock","ares_expand_name","ares_expand_string","ares_expand_string_ex"],"reason":"H0 only supplies arbitrary DNS bytes to ares_parse_*_reply and an arbitrary name to ares_create_query with fixed arguments. It never creates or operates an ares_channel, varies struct ares_options or optmask, exercises configuration-source precedence, advances asynchronous getaddrinfo state, or directly tests the public expansion APIs. S1 materially changes those uncovered semantics: init_by_options converts signed option fields such as options->tries, options->ndots, options->ednspsz, and options->udp_max_queries into size_t or unsigned fields; initialization replaces -1 sentinels with zero and changes override/default checks; next_dns_lookup compares a signed next_domain with channel->ndomains; ares_getsock adds behavior for numsocks <= 0; and ares_expand_name/ares_expand_string introduce explicit negative-alen handling and size_t-based internal paths. These are fuzz-worthy boundary, precedence, lifecycle, and signedness surfaces not reached by H0.","evidence":["ares-test-fuzz.c calls only ares_parse_a_reply, ares_parse_aaaa_reply, ares_parse_ptr_reply, ares_parse_ns_reply, ares_parse_srv_reply, ares_parse_mx_reply, ares_parse_txt_reply, ares_parse_soa_reply, ares_parse_naptr_reply, ares_parse_caa_reply, and ares_parse_uri_reply.","ares-test-fuzz-name.c calls only ares_create_query(name, C_IN, T_AAAA, 1234, 0, ..., 1024), so class, type, ID, flags, and maximum UDP size are fixed.","ares_init_options removes the -1 distinguished-value initialization, while ARES_CONFIG_CHECK and init_by_defaults now use positive/zero tests for nservers, ndots, timeout, and tries.","init_by_options casts options->flags to unsigned int and options->tries, options->ndots, options->ednspsz, and options->udp_max_queries to size_t or unsigned types.","set_options changes strtol-based signed parsing to strtoul for ndots:, retrans:, and retry:, and configuration precedence now depends on zero values and channel->optmask.","ares_getaddrinfo changes remaining, timeouts, and nodata_cnt to size_t and next_domain to ares_ssize_t; next_dns_lookup casts next_domain to size_t when comparing it with channel->ndomains.","ares_getsock now explicitly returns 0 when numsocks <= 0, but H0 never invokes a socket-processing API.","ares_expand_name and ares_expand_string retain signed int alen wrappers with new alen < 0 checks and delegate to size_t-based implementations; H0 never calls either public API directly."],"recommended_action":"Add a structured, stateful channel harness that fuzzes ares_init_options with independently varied optmask bits and boundary values for options->tries, ndots, timeout, ports, EDNS size, server/domain/sort counts, socket buffer sizes, and udp_max_queries; exercises configuration/default precedence, ares_getaddrinfo progression, ares_getsock with negative/zero/boundary numsocks, option save/duplication, and destruction. Add direct targets for ares_expand_name, ares_expand_string, and ares_expand_string_ex with valid in-buffer encoded offsets plus negative, zero, truncated, and boundary lengths."}
